/*!
\contentspage {Sailfish Accounts Contents}
\page index.html

\title Accessing online accounts with Sailfish Accounts

The Sailfish SDK includes Sailfish Accounts, a QML module for accessing accounts and
performing single-sign-on with accounts which the user adds via the system settings
application.

The Sailfish Accounts module is built on top of the Accounts&SSO framework described
in detail at \l{https://docs.accounts-sso.googlecode.com/git/libaccounts-qt/html/index.html}.
It provides some functionality which is not provided by the underlying library and also
provides a more QML friendly API.

\section1 Using Sailfish Accounts

To use Sailfish Accounts, you must import the module as follows:
\qml
import Sailfish.Accounts 1.0
\endqml

This will allow your application to use the types provided by Sailfish Accounts, including:
\list
\li \l{Account}
\li \l{SignInParameters}
\li \l{AccountModel}
\li \l{Service}
\li \l{ServiceType}
\li \l{Provider}
\li \l{ProviderModel}
\li \l{AccountManager}
\endlist

Please see the documentation of each of the types above for in-depth information on
how to create application-specific credentials associated with an account and sign
in to the online service using those credentials.

The Sailfish Accounts module also provides some UI elements which allow accounts
to be selected for further use:
\list
\li \l{AccountProviderPicker}
\li \l{AccountProviderPickerDialog}
\li \l{AccountsListView}
\endlist

*/